
// =============================================================================
// NIRI — INPUT CONFIGURATION
// =============================================================================
//
// Purpose:
//   Apply shared input preferences using native Niri settings.
//
// Shared preferences originate from:
//   user/preferences/input.nix
//
// How generation works:
//
//   1. default.nix reads this file as a KDL template.
//   2. The Nix input adapter imports preferences/input.nix.
//   3. It generates Niri input and cursor configuration.
//   4. The generated configuration replaces the marker below.
//   5. Home Manager installs the completed file.
//
// Shared settings include:
//
//   - Natural touchpad scrolling
//   - Natural mouse scrolling
//   - Focus behavior
//   - Scrolling unfocused windows
//   - Hide pointer while typing
//   - Hide pointer after 3000 ms
//
// Important:
//   Not all user preferences require an explicit native setting.
//   Some behavior may already be Niri's default.
//
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// GENERATED SHARED INPUT SETTINGS
// =============================================================================
//
// The adapter generates the required input and cursor blocks here.
//
// For example, the requested three-second pointer timeout should become:
//
//   cursor {
//       hide-when-typing
//       hide-after-inactive-ms 3000
//   }
//
// Natural scrolling is generated separately for mouse and touchpad.
//
// Do not manually duplicate shared preferences outside this marker.

// @SHARED_INPUT@


// =============================================================================
// NIRI-SPECIFIC INPUT SETTINGS
// =============================================================================
//
// Add behavior here only when it is specific to Niri.
//
// Possible future additions:
//   - Niri-specific device overrides
//   - Special touchpad behavior
//   - Tablet or drawing-device support
//
// IMPORTANT:
//   Avoid creating duplicate top-level input or cursor sections
//   without verifying Niri's merging behavior.
//
// Shared values should continue to originate from input.nix.
